HST Office: no engine version in the remaining texts users can see.

hst-version-everywhere.patch put the HST release in About, `soffice --version`, document
metadata, PDF/EPS/HTML and Windows file versions. Three places still showed the engine version
(26.8 / 26.8.1.1):

- The ReadMe (readmes/README_<lang>, "HST Office 26.8 ReadMe"): ${PRODUCTVERSION} is the HST
  major.minor of include/hst_version.h (scripts/write-hst-version.py), e.g. "HST Office 1.0".
  The header is a prerequisite, so a new /VERSION rebuilds the ReadMe; a missing header stops
  the ReadMe rule with a message instead of falling back to the engine version.
- The UI string hooks: %ABOUTBOXPRODUCTVERSION is the HST release and %PRODUCTEXTENSION /
  %ABOUTBOXPRODUCTVERSIONSUFFIX are empty in the office (desktop/source/app/app.cxx), and the
  standalone Extension Manager (unopkg gui) expands %PRODUCTVERSION and the others like the
  office does.
- Extension dependency errors named the engine version an extension declares
  ("Extension requires at least HST Office version 27.2"): the LibreOffice-minimal/maximal
  messages now say only that a newer / another version of HST Office is needed. The check
  itself is unchanged.

Kept internal on purpose: utl::ConfigManager::getProductVersion()/getAboutBoxProductVersion()
and ooSetupVersion* (extension dependency checks, LIBO_VERSION for themes and extensions,
Windows accessibility toolkit version, Impress Remote protocol, the HTTP User-Agent of WebDAV,
CMIS and LanguageTool requests).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

